  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... \nWinds will continue to be the main weather concern throughout \nSaturday morning with gusts between 30-35 in southern and central \nArizona, but should remain below advisory level winds. However, \nanother round of advisory level winds are expect in Yuma County \nand southern La Paz County Saturday morning, but currently \nallowing the earlier advisory to expire before reissuing to avoid \nconfusion. \n\nAside from the wind concern, guidance is suggesting some lower \nend shower potential over the weekend. The placement of the cut- \noff low to our southwest starting Friday is expected to advect a \ndecent mid and upper level moisture into the area. Some high-based\nlight showers may become possible across southern Arizona as \nearly as Friday evening with best chances Saturday afternoon as \nthe cut-off low weakens and migrates over the region. Unfortunately,\nlittle if any measurable rainfall is expected, as most locations \nwill struggle to get anything more than a trace to a few \nhundredths of an inch. The good news though will be around a 5F-6F\ndecrease in afternoon highs on Saturday, so expect highs in the \nlow 80s across the lower deserts.\n \nBy early next week, weak upper level riding will effect the \nregion, resuming near normal temperatures. Looking out even \nfurther, ensemble guidance is hinting at another deep Pacific \ntrough moving into the Western U.S. early next week and \npotentially reaching our region during the middle part of next \nweek. This next weather system could bring more rain chances and \nanother cool down during the latter half of next week.",
